WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:05.820
Hello, everyone, and welcome to your second drink of email surveillance.
大家好，欢迎来到你们的第二杯“邮件监控”节目。

2
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:10.220
In our breakdown this week, we have a fantastic interview with Ken Jeong.
在本周的解析中，我们请到了肯·郑（Ken Jeong）进行了一场精彩的访谈。

3
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.600
With a pop-in from Joel McHale.
乔尔·麦克哈尔（Joel McHale）也来客串了一下。

4
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:16.340
Yeah, these were the old days when a bunch of us were all recording at the same time.
没错，那是我们很多人同时录音的旧时光。

5
00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:20.680
Yes, and then we'd see people going from one podcast to another.
是的，那时候我们还会看到大家从一个播客串到另一个播客。

6
00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:21.800
It was a lot of fun.
那真的很有趣。

7
00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:29.580
Well, in this episode, Email Surveillance, we get to see Michael Scott go to his improv class.
在这一集《邮件监控》中，我们看到迈克尔·斯科特去上了即兴表演课。

8
00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:30.880
Oh, it's so delicious.
哦，那真是太精彩了。

9
00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:31.820
So good.
太棒了。

10
00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:38.360
And, you know, when he's in improv class, he turns every scene into a Michael Skarn moment.
而且，你知道，当他在即兴表演课上时，他会把每一场戏都变成迈克尔·斯卡恩（Michael Skarn）的时刻。

11
00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:41.760
He pulls out his imaginary gun and he shoots them.
他会掏出他的假想枪，然后把他们都射杀。

12
00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:47.420
Well, in his interview, Ken Jeong shared some really fun stuff about shooting all those scenes.
在访谈中，肯·郑分享了一些拍摄那些场景时非常有趣的事情。

13
00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:54.560
But I found an interview that Steve did with Janelle Riley for the Screen Actors Foundation,
但我找到了史蒂夫（Steve）接受珍妮尔·莱利（Janelle Riley）为演员工会基金会（Screen Actors Foundation）做的采访，

14
00:00:54.560 --> 00:01:01.080
where he explained the inspiration for Michael's character always pulling a gun,
他在采访中解释了迈克尔这个角色在即兴表演课上总是掏枪的灵感来源，

15
00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:02.380
in an improv class.
是在即兴表演课上。

16
00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:05.340
It was based on a real person.
这是基于一个真实的人。

17
00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:06.480
Yes.
是的。

18
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:07.640
Let's listen.
我们来听听看。

19
00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:11.720
I know on The Office, Michael Scott was a big fan of improv.
我知道在《办公室》里，迈克尔·斯科特是个即兴表演的忠实粉丝。

20
00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:12.200
Yeah.
没错。

21
00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:16.260
And his improvs were angry, but he was always pulling a gun.
他的即兴表演总是充满愤怒，而且他总是会掏出一把枪。

22
00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.120
That's actually, that's based on a friend of mine.
那其实是基于我的一个朋友。

23
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:19.960
Oh, is it really?
哦，真的吗？

24
00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:20.280
Not.
不是。

25
00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:24.060
There was a guy at Second City who always used to pull a gun during scenes.
在第二城市（Second City）剧团有个家伙，他以前在表演时总是会掏枪。

26
00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:27.000
And he knows it.
而且他自己也知道。

27
00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:28.540
And he'll laugh about it, too.
他也会拿这件事开玩笑。

28
00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:34.340
But we actually let him, a scene got into the show in Second City because we all agreed,
但我们确实让他演过，有一场戏被放进了第二城市的演出里，因为我们都商量好了，

29
00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:39.540
we're going to let Ron pull the gun and then we're going to let him kill all of us in the scene.
我们要让罗恩（Ron）掏枪，然后我们要让他把戏里的我们全都杀掉。

30
00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.480
And that's what the scene was.
那场戏就是这样的。

31
00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:43.160
That really made me laugh.
这真的让我大笑不止。

32
00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:45.580
I mean, it took me back to my improv days.
我是说，这让我回想起了我自己的即兴表演时光。

33
00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:50.040
Well, if you're like me and you wanted more scenes from that improv class,
好吧，如果你和我一样，想看更多那场即兴表演课的片段，

34
00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:52.560
there are a lot more in deleted scenes.
在删减片段里还有很多。

35
00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:53.620
Let's hear some.
我们来听听看。

36
00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:58.280
I need to know who shot Johnson.
我需要知道是谁杀了约翰逊。

37
00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:00.900
President Johnson.
约翰逊总统。

38
00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:03.080
Shut up.
闭嘴。

39
00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:03.560
Okay.
好的。

40
00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:08.420
I have a right mind to shoot you right in the head.
我真想一枪崩了你的头。

41
00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:09.900
I killed him.
是我杀了他。

42
00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:10.440
You're right.
你说得对。

43
00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:11.240
It was me.
是我干的。

44
00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:12.540
Just shut up.
闭嘴吧。

45
00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:14.280
I don't want to hear anything more from you.
我不想再听你废话了。

46
00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:15.520
No, listen to what she's saying.
不，听听她在说什么。

47
00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:18.690
All right.
好吧。

48
00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:20.710
I'll be quiet if we can make some kind of deal.
如果我们能达成某种交易，我就安静下来。

49
00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:22.270
A deal?
交易？

50
00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:24.190
Pow, pow, pow, pow.
砰，砰，砰，砰。

51
00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:25.010
No deals.
没得谈。

52
00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:27.490
Not with Michael Skarn, FBI.
别想跟FBI的迈克尔·斯卡恩谈。

53
00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:29.850
Michael Skarn doesn't make deals.
迈克尔·斯卡恩从不交易。

54
00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:33.830
Michael Skarn shoots and then asks questions later.
迈克尔·斯卡恩只管开枪，事后再问话。

55
00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:37.240
Good.
很好。

56
00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:38.560
Good.
很好。

57
00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:40.680
Guess what?
你猜怎么着？

58
00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:44.780
Michael Skarn is now alone on stage because he no longer has any scene partners.
迈克尔·斯卡恩现在独自站在舞台上，因为他已经没有搭档了。

59
00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:48.300
I re-watched all these deleted scenes too.
我也把这些删减片段全重看了一遍。

60
00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:56.040
And after that moment, he gets in this whole argument with the teacher and the student about how she wasn't doing the scene right.
在那之后，他和老师还有学生吵了一架，说她演得不对。

61
00:02:56.340 --> 00:03:01.060
The teacher is trying to like gently suggest that that could have gone another way.
老师试图委婉地建议，说那场戏其实可以有别的演法。

62
00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:01.360
Right.
没错。

63
00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:06.760
And Michael's like, well, it could have gone another way if we wanted to do it not funny, basically.
迈克尔就说，如果我们不想演得好笑，那确实可以有别的演法。

64
00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.220
Like, that's his whole thing.
他就是这样的人。

65
00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:10.320
He's like such a horrible scene partner.
他真是个糟糕的搭档。

66
00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:18.480
Well, there is another deleted scene, which they actually added to the superfan episode where the teacher tells everyone to partner up.
对了，还有一个删减片段，被加进了超级粉丝版剧集里，老师让大家两两分组。

67
00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:20.500
But no one wants to partner with Michael.
但没人想和迈克尔一组。

68
00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:22.740
He just, well, why would they?
他就是……好吧，谁会想跟他一组呢？

69
00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:23.240
No.
没人。

70
00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:29.780
So he just keeps shouting out suggestions and then the teacher keeps suggesting, you know what, why don't you take a break?
所以他不停地大喊建议，老师就一直劝他，你知道吗，要不你先休息一下？

71
00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:30.900
It's really funny.
真的很好笑。

72
00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:34.380
All of these scenes, you know, brought me back to my improv days.
所有这些片段，让我回想起了我即兴表演的日子。

73
00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:40.600
I mean, I feel like I've shared with you how we had one guy who would steamroll every scene he was in.
我是说，我好像跟你们分享过，我们当时有个家伙，不管演什么戏都要强行主导。

74
00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:44.560
So we all just made a pact that in every scene we'd find a way to kill him.
所以我们大家私下约定，在每一场戏里都要想办法“杀掉”他。

75
00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:47.500
Oh, you were Michael Skarning him.
噢，你们是在对他进行“迈克尔·斯卡恩式”对待啊。

76
00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:48.080
In reverse.
反向的。

77
00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:48.600
Yeah.
没错。

78
00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:51.040
But you would, everyone got so creative.
但你们真的，每个人都变得好有创意。

79
00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:55.620
There were blow darts, attack of a killer cat.
有吹箭，还有杀人猫袭击。

80
00:03:57.080 --> 00:04:05.700
Well, you know, this is also the episode where Jim is throwing a party at his house and Michael finds out that he's not invited.
对了，这一集里吉姆在家里办派对，迈克尔发现自己没被邀请。

81
00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:07.620
I know.
我知道。

82
00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:11.600
There's actually a lot of discussion about who is invited and who is going.
关于谁被邀请了、谁要去参加，其实有很多讨论。

83
00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:19.640
And Angela, in our breakdown, you mentioned how at five minutes and 57 seconds, we see the invite on Michael's computer.
安吉拉，在我们的解析里，你提到在5分57秒时，我们看到了迈克尔电脑上的邀请函。

84
00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:20.880
We see the invitation.
我们看到了那份邀请。

85
00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:23.920
Well, a new catch.
好吧，有个新发现。

86
00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:25.360
I have a new catch.
我有个新发现。

87
00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:34.480
If you look closely, you can see that the Evite says 14 people have said yes to the Evite and two have not replied.
如果你仔细看，可以看到电子邀请函上显示有14人确认参加，2人未回复。

88
00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:42.200
Now, we can only see who said yes, but Pam is not on the liSt.
现在我们只能看到谁确认了，但名单里没有帕姆。

89
00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:44.480
Has she not replied?
她还没回复吗？

90
00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:45.060
Maybe.
也许吧。

91
00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:48.580
But Pam has not confirmed her attendance.
但帕姆确实还没确认出席。

92
00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:54.880
Well, lady, I found another nugget that might explain why Pam hasn't RSVP'd yet.
好吧，女士，我发现了另一个可能解释为什么帕姆还没回复的小细节。

93
00:04:55.100 --> 00:05:00.040
I wonder if it's because she didn't know she was RSVPing for one or two people.
我在想是不是因为她不知道该按一个人还是两个人的名额回复。

94
00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:04.980
When we broke down this episode, we were speculating why Roy wasn't at Jim's barbecue.
我们解析这一集时，还在猜测为什么罗伊没去吉姆的烧烤派对。

95
00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:10.860
Well, the reason Roy doesn't go is a deleted scene, and it was added to the superfan episode.
其实罗伊没去的原因在一个删减片段里，它被加进了超级粉丝版剧集。

96
00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:11.860
It's great.
太棒了。

97
00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:12.720
Let's hear it.
让我们听听看。

98
00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:13.280
Hi.
嗨。

99
00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:13.920
Hey, babe.
嘿，宝贝。

100
00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:14.260
Hey.
嘿。

101
00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:14.540
Hey.
嘿。

102
00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:15.440
How are you?
你好吗？

103
00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:15.980
Good.
挺好的。

104
00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:17.180
You look good.
你看上去气色不错。

105
00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:22.060
Um, I was wondering if it might be okay if I go to Lonnie's poker game tonight.
嗯，我在想，今晚我能不能去参加朗尼的扑克局？

106
00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:24.280
I promise it'll be like the last time for a while.
我保证这会是近期最后一次了。

107
00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:26.840
We're supposed to go to the barbecue at Jim's house.
我们本来要去吉姆家参加烧烤聚会的。

108
00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:28.640
Oh, man.
噢，天哪。

109
00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:31.300
Um, could you go without me?
嗯，你能自己去吗？

110
00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:35.380
Make something up, say I'm like, ate something, or...
随便编个理由，就说我吃了什么不舒服之类的，或者……

111
00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:36.220
Huh?
啊？

112
00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:36.640
Huh?
啊？

113
00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:38.060
You're the beSt.
你最好了。

114
00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:39.220
You're the beSt.
你最好了。

115
00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:40.700
I might be late.
我可能会晚点回来。

116
00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:42.720
Okay, don't wake me up, because I'm playing ball in the morning.
行，别叫醒我，因为我明天早上还要打球。

117
00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:43.260
Okay.
好吧。

118
00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:43.920
All right.
行吧。

119
00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:44.160
Bye.
再见。

120
00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:49.200
Did you hear that?
你听到了吗？

121
00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:49.580
Yeah.
听到了。

122
00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:52.120
How he like butters her up before he ditches her for the night?
他为了晚上能溜出去，是怎么哄她的？

123
00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:53.540
Then says you're the beSt.
然后还说你最好了。

124
00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:54.760
Also, don't wake me up.
还有，别叫醒我。

125
00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:55.040
Yeah.
是啊。

126
00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:56.440
And he has to play ball in the morning.
而且他明天早上还得打球。

127
00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:57.300
He's busy.
他很忙。

128
00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:58.340
He's got a lot going on.
他有很多事要忙。

129
00:05:58.480 --> 00:05:59.700
And none of it is with Pam.
而且没一件是陪帕姆的。

130
00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:00.440
None of it.
一件都没有。

131
00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:04.040
Well, everyone, that is your second drink for today.
好了，各位，这是你们今天的第二杯酒了。

132
00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:06.280
And now, here is email surveillance.
现在，进入邮件监控环节。

133
00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:11.650
I'm Jenna Fischer.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

134
00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:12.930
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

135
00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:14.210
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演过《办公室》。

136
00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:15.450
And we're best friends.
我们也是最好的朋友。

137
00:06:15.530 --> 00:06:19.270
And now, we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你带来《办公室》终极重温播客。

138
00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:23.630
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes
每周，我们都会解析一集《办公室》，并分享独家幕后故事，

139
00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:26.250
stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
这些故事只有我们这两个亲历者才能告诉你。

140
00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:27.430
We're the Office Ladies.
我们是《办公室女士》。

141
00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:35.860
To the email surveillance episode of Office Ladies.
欢迎收听《办公室女士》之邮件监控那一集。

142
00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:36.680
Howdy!
大家好！

143
00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:41.420
It is Season 2, Episode 9, written by Jen Salata, directed by Paul Feig.
这是第二季第九集，由简·萨拉塔编剧，保罗·费格执导。

144
00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:43.500
And we have a special guest in the studio with us today.
今天我们演播室里有一位特别嘉宾。

145
00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:48.020
He played Bill, one of the members of Michael Scott's improv class.
他饰演了比尔，迈克尔·斯科特即兴表演课的成员之一。

146
00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:50.600
It is our friend, Kin Jong!
他就是我们的朋友，金·钟！

147
00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:52.260
Hey, guys.
嘿，大家好。

148
00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:54.760
Thank you so much for having me.
非常感谢邀请我来。

149
00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:56.840
We are so excited you are here.
我们很高兴你能来。

150
00:06:56.840 --> 00:06:58.520
You are our second in-studio gueSt.
你是我们第二位演播室嘉宾。

151
00:06:58.680 --> 00:06:59.160
Yes!
太棒了！

152
00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:01.680
You and Creed Bratton, Kin.
你和克里德·布拉顿（Creed Bratton）在一起，金。

153
00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:03.660
That is privileged company.
那可是了不起的同伴。

154
00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:06.380
So, I'm very, very excited to be here.
所以我非常、非常高兴能来到这里。

155
00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:07.780
So, seriously, thank you guys.
说真的，谢谢你们。

156
00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:08.440
And congrats.
还有，恭喜。

157
00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:10.520
